<title>BELGIUM: Belgian sugar beet drilling jumps in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian sugar beet drilling jumps in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian sugar beet plantings surged to 97.7 percent of the total planned area on April 14, from 71.69 percent the previous week, the Belgian sugar beet institute (IRBAB) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The institute gave no figure for the area planted so far because data from four of the nine factories were not yet available.</p>
<p>The planned area for 1997 is 102,262 hectares, down from 103,849 in 1996.</p>
<p>--Brussels Newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
